{number: 123}
{title: Father God Will I Know}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G] Father God, will I know you are gracious,
And I [C] know of your love for all [G] men,
Will I know that your love never changes,
There is [D7] hope for the ones yet in [G] sin.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [C] Lord fill me now with Thy [G] Spirit,
As I [D7] wait, fill me now Lord I [G] pray,
Till the [C] fire of your Spirit con-[G] sumes me,
Fill my [D7] heart in your own special [G] way.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
By the [G] power of the spirit within me,
Cleanse my [C] heart of the black stains of [G] sin,
Till my heart burns no more in its passion,
Till my [D7] longings are holy and [G] clean.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Lord I [G] know that you died for the sinner,
That your [C] death gave new hope to all [G] men,
As in power from the tomb you ascended,
So in [D7] power come upon us a-[G] gain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Till the [G] earth is rolled up like a garment,
Till the [C] end of this age comes to [G] be;
Let us cease not our praise nor thanksgiving,
Let us [D7] thank Him for setting us [G] free.
{end_of_verse}
